      "word": "DIZEN",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To dress; to attire. [Obs.] Beau. & Fl.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To dress gaudily; to overdress; to bedizen; to deck out. Like a tragedy queen, he has dizened her out. Goldsmith. To-morrow when the masks shall fall That dizen Nature's carnival. Emerson.",
